Fiddler — https://github.com/efeslab/fiddler
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

  `src/fiddler_baseline/mixtral.py` is a lightly modified copy of Fiddler, used
  as the quantitative baseline in the paper. The modifications are:
    - the expert popularity source is configurable (FS_POPULARITY_JSON)
    - the offload constants are configurable (FS_LATENCY_CPU, FS_LATENCY_GPU)
    - the number of cached experts can be forced (FS_FORCE_EXPERTS), which the
      paper uses to measure the memory floor with the cache emptied
    - peak and process GPU memory are reported
  None of these changes alter the placement or offload policy.

  `src/fiddlestick/mixtral.py` builds on the same code base and adds the
  contribution of this work: sequential in-place streaming of the non-expert
  layers, double buffered over a dedicated CUDA stream.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DAOP — https://github.com/ecolab-nus/DAOP, commit 08fef33
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Not redistributed here.

  `patches/daop_instrumentation.patch` is the unified diff applied to an
  unmodified checkout so that the comparison in the paper can be reproduced.
  It makes the input/output token grid and the beam width configurable by
  environment variable, lets the offload constants be supplied externally so
  that DAOP and this work use the same measured values, and adds peak memory,
  process GPU memory and expert cache hit-rate counters.

  The patch changes no part of DAOP's algorithm. In particular DAOP's
  brute-force search over expert placements is left exactly as published.

